{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ed7e39d99b57bc5acd", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Waves and Sound - Test 2", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfe5"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfa0", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf39", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["6117b76e478ae845c43c6e13"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d30"], "question": {"text": "A heavy ball of mass <math><mi>M</mi></math> is suspended from the ceiling of a car by a light string of mass <math><mi>m</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&#8810;</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> When the car is at rest, the speed of transverse waves in the string is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> When the car has acceleration <math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the wave-speed increases to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60.5</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> The value of <math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo></math> in terms of gravitational acceleration <math><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo></math> is closed to"}, "options": [{"id": "571bec", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf3a"}, {"id": "0c6b18", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf3b"}, {"id": "61f95a", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf3c"}, {"id": "d80a59", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf3d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf3e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f38"], "concepts": ["655b98d00acb2d1c8296e568"], "question": {"text": "A sinusoidal wave of wavelength 7.5 cm travels a distance of 1.2 cm along the x -direction in 0.3 sec. The crest $P$ is at $x=0$ at $t=0 \\mathrm{sec}$ and maximum displacement of the wave is 2 cm. Which equation correctly represents this wave ?"}, "options": [{"id": "7858a1", "text": "$y=2 \\cos (0.83 x-3.35 t) \\mathrm{cm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf3f"}, {"id": "49ab2e", "text": "$y=2 \\sin (0.83 x-3.5 t) \\mathrm{cm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf40"}, {"id": "43c151", "text": "$y=2 \\cos (3.35 x-0.83 t) \\mathrm{cm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf41"}, {"id": "03fc3f", "text": "$y=2 \\cos (0.13 x-0.5 t) \\mathrm{cm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf42"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4