 src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F65dd588d-1897-49dc-ad9b-bedbd5efd228-image17.png?alt=media\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "ece094", "text": "<math><mi> </mi><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>:</mo><mn>5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf58"}, {"id": "8d371f", "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>:</mo><mn>9</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf59"}, {"id": "6b51e8", "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf5a"}, {"id": "d1f75b", "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf5b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf5c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f38"], "concepts": ["6162fb146ed13040ec84acd7"], "question": {"text": "A sound wave of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>245</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> travels with the speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> along the positive x-axis. Each point of the wave moves to and fro through a total distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. What will be the mathematical expression of this travelling wave?"}, "options": [{"id": "3ae511", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>x<