on. A transverse wave is then made to pass through both the strings. The velocity of the wave in the first string having the radius of cross section R is $\\mathrm{v}_1$, and that in the other string having radius of cross section $R / 2$ is $v_2$. Then $\\frac{v_2}{v_1}=$"}, "options": [{"id": "06e6b2", "text": "$\\sqrt{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf62"}, {"id": "d35349", "text": "2", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf63"}, {"id": "cafae1", "text": "8", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf64"}, {"id": "98c9f9", "text": "4", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf65"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4eefc677dc36a88ecf66", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["6117b76e478ae845c43c6e13"], "concepts": ["6162fb136ed13040ec84abdd"], "question": {"text": "A longitudinal wave is represented by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The maximum particle velocity will be four times the wave velocity if the determined value of wavelength is equal to"}, "options": [{"id": "0d9e16", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf67"}, {"id": "1e2302", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf68"}, {"id": "6c7f9e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf69"}, {"id": "474c95", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf6a"}], "questi