<mi>z</mi></math>, then&nbsp;s &nbsp;will be of the order of (take the multiplicative constant to be 1 )"}, "options": [{"id": "ac8d18", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>mm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf80"}, {"id": "6bffae", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf81"}, {"id": "38ec77", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mi>mm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf82"}, {"id": "fdfa43", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf83"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf84", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475b"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b470f"], "question": {"text": "In the resonance experiment, two air columns (closed at one end) of 100 cm and 120 cm long, give 15 beats per second when each one is sounding in the respective fundamental modes. The velocity of sound in the air column is :"}, "options": [{"id": "c7535c", "text": "$335 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf85"}, {"id": "2ff3ff", "text": "$370 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf86"}, {"id": "b084ca", "text": "$340 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf87"}, {"id": "fc5876", "text": "$360 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf88"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf89", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["6162fb156ed13040ec84ade8"], "concepts": ["6162fb156ed13040ec84adc0"], "question": {"text": "Sound travels in a mixture of two moles of helium and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> moles of hydrogen. If rms speed of gas molecules in the mixture is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math> times the speed of sound, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> will be"}, "options": [{"id": "81857f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf8a"}, {"id": "0c0c02", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf8b"}, {"id": "ba43d1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf8c"}, {"id": "67796b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf8d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf8e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e567ac499d1e49588f95ea"], "concepts": ["60e567aa499d1e49588f95c1"], "question": {"text": "Two harmonic waves moving in the same direction superimpose to form a wave $\\mathrm{x}=\\mathrm{a} \\cos (1.5 \\mathrm{t}) \\cos (50.5 \\mathrm{t})$ where $t$ is in seconds. Find the period with which they beat (close to nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "b4ebc7", "text": "6 s", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf8f"}, {"id": "ce915a", "text": "4 s", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf90"}, {"id": "65d602", "text": "1 s", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf91"}, {"id": "0cf3da", "text": "2 s", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf92"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf93", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f38"], "concepts": ["6162fb146ed13040ec84acd3"], "question": {"text": "A travelling harmonic wave is represented by the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>sin</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>50</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mtext>,</mtext></math> where <math><mi>x</mi></math> and <math><mi>y</mi></math> are in meter and <math><mi>t</mi></math> is in seconds. Which of the following is a correct statement about the wave?"}, "options": [{"id": "47543b", "text": "The wave is propagating along the positive <math><mi>x</mi></math> -axis with speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf94"}, {"id": "c16f3a", "text": "The wave is propagating along the positive <math><mi>x</mi></math> -axis with speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf95"}, {"id": "1d4572", "text": "The wave is propagating along the negative <math><mi>x</mi></math> -axis with speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf96"}, {"id": "8bf0fe", "text": "The wave is propagating along the negative <math><mi>x</mi></math> -axis with speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf97"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf98", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475b"], "concepts": ["60e08778d7588a2678f93ba0"], "question": {"text": "A closed organ and an open organ tube are filled by two different gases having same bulk modulus but different densities $\\rho_1$ and $\\rho_{2^{\\prime}}$, respectively. The frequency of $9^{\\text {th }}$ harmonic of closed tube is identical with $4^{\\text {th }}$ harmonic of open tube. If the length of the closed tube is 10 cm and the density ratio of the gases is $\\rho_1: \\rho_2=1: 16$, then the length of the open tube is :"}, "options": [{"id": "7968fa", "text": "$\\frac{15}{7} \\mathrm{~cm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf99"}, {"id": "983270", "text": "$\\frac{20}{7} \\mathrm{~cm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf9a"}, {"id": "8f4f07", "text": "$\\frac{15}{9} \\mathrm{~cm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf9b"}, {"id": "474b00", "text": "$\\frac{20}{9} \\mathrm{~cm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecf9c"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:00.017Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:00.017Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfe3"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfe1", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfc5", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475b"], "concepts": ["60e08778d7588a2678f93ba0"], "question": {"text": "An organ pipe <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> long is open at both ends. The speed of sound in air is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>360</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The frequency of the second harmonic is _<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi><mo>.</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "63fddf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfc6"}, {"id": "d02e70", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfc7"}, {"id": "0cd0e8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfc8"}, {"id": "99d46c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfc9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfca", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["6117b76e478ae845c43c6e13"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d30"], "question": {"text": "The mass per unit length of a uniform wire is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>135</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. A transverse wave of the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>21</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is produced in it, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is in meter and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is in second. Then, the expected value of tension in the wire is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. Value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is <u>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</u>&nbsp;(Round-off to the nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "1facc0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfcb"}, {"id": "9e610b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfcc"}, {"id": "e9cd7d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfcd"}, {"id": "c30ce6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfce"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfcf", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f38"], "concepts": ["61923f37d42d105914c0fca9"], "question": {"text": "A point source is emitting sound waves of intensity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> at the origin. The difference in intensity (magnitude only) at two points located at a distances of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> from the origin respectively will be ________<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "46ad4e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfd0"}, {"id": "c74ffb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfd1"}, {"id": "464d38", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfd2"}, {"id": "63cb5f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfd3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfd4", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e567ac499d1e49588f95ea"], "concepts": ["60e567aa499d1e49588f95c1"], "question": {"text": "A set of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math> tuning forks is arranged in a series of increasing frequencies. If each fork gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> beats with respect to the preceding fork and the frequency of the last fork is twice the frequency of the first, then the frequency of last fork is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Hz</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "243925", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfd5"}, {"id": "4dd373", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfd6"}, {"id": "52a4ca", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfd7"}, {"id": "3ef2a1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfd8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88ecfd9", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d491b"], "topics": ["60e56769499d1e49588f8f06"], "concepts": ["60da9e95bce5511ac09ad99e"], "question": {"text": "<p>The displacement equations of two interfering waves are given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow